<p>"Anomalous region" Why you cheeky —!</p>
<p>Anyway, I still think anomalous is chintzy and unnecessary. ;-p</p>
<p>On further thought, I'd suggest that 301 be triggered by density — density of mass/energy basically. Otherwise, it seems like the region would constantly be sucking in gas, light, energy, etc. With no minimum limit, it should suck in any matter and energy that enters it. If that were the case, it'd be very noticeable.</p>
<p>The benefit a density trigger gives you is it provides a filter which keeps 301 from going off constantly.</p>
<p><em>Yeah, I just now noticed the bit about how 301 closes itself up when it has matter in it. Sorry for being dense — I still think you should consider a density trigger, though.</em></p>

