														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1731066">
									

<p>Density is kind of an odd trigger for this phenomenon, given that it is an average measurement for a given area and not necessarily an intrinsic property. I mean, yes, normal air isn't very dense when you look at a container of it, but the individual atoms of nitrogen or oxygen themselves are not significantly less dense than they would be incorporated into a solid object. Perhaps size IS a better cutoff than density after all.</p>

